{"id": "section-body-22596", "title": "CKD Associated Anaemia", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-one", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "KIDNEY AND UROLOGICAL DISORDERS", "Hypertension and CKD", "CKD Associated Anaemia"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-22596", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "CKD Associated Anaemia", "runs": [{"text": "CKD"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Anaemia"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "666"}}, {"id": "body-22597", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Patients with CKD present with anemia due to erythropoietin deficiency, iron deficiency due to low iron stores, and impaired iron utilization due to inflammation. Other causes include shortened red blood cell lifespan due to Uremic toxins, nutritional deficiencies, such as folate and vitamin B12, and blood loss due to frequent blood draws, gastrointestinal bleeding, or dialysis- related blood loss further decreases red blood cell counts. [Refer to the national guidelines for dialysis]", "runs": [{"text": "Patients with CKD present with anemia due to erythropoietin deficiency, iron deficiency due to low iron stores, and impaired iron utilization due to inflammation. Other causes include shortened red blood cell lifespan due to Uremic toxins, nutritional deficiencies,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "folate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vitamin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "B12,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loss"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "frequent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "draws,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gastrointestinal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bleeding,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dialysis- rela